# Certs generated by ca/generate.sh — never commit private keys
certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# SFTP runtime directories (make sftp-dirs). sftp/config/ is tracked --
# it holds the seeded merchant-onboarding.json, not runtime output.
/sftp/out/
/sftp/staging/
/sftp/outbound/
/sftp/inbound/
/sftp/archive/

# Console registry (make up creates it world-writable; merchants you create
# in the UI live here, and they are lab data, not source)
/console-data/

# B4B's boarding + payout state (companies, people, beneficiaries,
# payments). Lab data, same as the console registry.
/b4b-data/

# Pod runtime output (CWD-relative, recipe-relative, or a test's package
# directory). Must not be anchored to the repo root: `go test ./core/pod`
# wrote keys under core/pod/pod-data/.
pod-data/

# Go
bin/
dist/
vendor/
*.test
coverage.out

# `go build ./...` from the repo root drops one binary per cmd/ package
# here, named after the package. Four of them were committed by accident
# (~35MB of ELF in a source repo); these keep it from happening again.
# Note there is no /worldline entry: that is a real, tracked directory
# holding the settlement-file fixtures, and `go build ./...` fails on it
# rather than overwriting it. Build into a path instead: go build -o /tmp/x ./cmd/...
/aci
/b4b
/bank
/bankingcircle
/console
/harness
/notifier
/paymentapi
/receiver
/settlement
/verify

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Compose leftovers
.compose-ready

# openssl leftovers if generated in-tree
*.srl


.claude
